"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoodpecker=self.webpackChunkwoodpecker||[]).push([["5693"],{7038(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"name":"OpenArtifact","slug":"openartifact","url":"https://github.com/openartifact/drone-openartifact","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openartifact/drone-openartifact/refs/heads/main/images/logo.svg","description":"Plugin to upload artifacts to OpenArtifact and promote releases","docs":"<p>The OpenArtifact plugin uploads build artifacts to an <a href=\\"https://github.com/openartifact/openartifact\\">OpenArtifact</a> server, records the pipeline (build number, URL, commit) on every file, and promotes release bundles between stages. It wraps the <code>oa</code> CLI, so it needs OpenArtifact 0.10.0 or newer. The below pipeline configuration demonstrates simple usage:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">steps:\\n  - name: upload\\n    image: ghcr.io/openartifact/drone-openartifact\\n    settings:\\n      server: https://artifacts.example.com\\n      token:\\n        from_secret: openartifact_token\\n      repo: releases\\n      files:\\n        - dist/*.tar.gz\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>Example configuration for a Drone pipeline (the same settings apply, secrets use <code>from_secret</code> as well):</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-yaml\\">kind: pipeline\\ntype: docker\\nname: default\\n\\nsteps:\\n  - name: upload\\n    image: ghcr.io/openartifact/drone-openartifact\\n    settings:\\n      server: https://artifacts.example.com\\n      token:\\n        from_secret: openartifact_token\\n      repo: releases\\n      files:\\n        - dist/*.tar.gz\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>Example configuration with a target path, flat uploads and custom properties:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-diff\\">  - name: upload\\n    image: ghcr.io/openartifact/drone-openartifact\\n    settings:\\n      server: https://artifacts.example.com\\n      token:\\n        from_secret: openartifact_token\\n      repo: releases\\n      files:\\n        - dist/*.tar.gz\\n+     target_path: myapp/${CI_COMMIT_TAG}\\n+     flat: true\\n+     properties:\\n+       team: core\\n+       channel: stable\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>Example configuration that uploads on a tag, seals a release bundle with everything this pipeline uploaded and promotes it to the <code>prod</code> stage:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-diff\\">  - name: release\\n    image: ghcr.io/openartifact/drone-openartifact\\n+   when:\\n+     event: tag\\n    settings:\\n      server: https://artifacts.example.com\\n      token:\\n        from_secret: openartifact_token\\n      repo: releases\\n      files:\\n        - dist/*.tar.gz\\n+     action: upload+promote\\n+     bundle_pipeline: release\\n+     stage: prod\\n+     notes: Released by CI\\n+     result_file: openartifact-result.json\\n</code></pre>\\n<p>Example configuration that promotes an already sealed bundle, for example from a manually triggered pipeline:</p>\\n<pre><code class=\\"language-diff\\">  - name: promote\\n    image: ghcr.io/openartifact/drone-openartifact\\n    settings:\\n      server: https://artifacts.example.com\\n      token:\\n        from_secret: openartifact_token\\n+     action: promote\\n+     bundle_name: myapp\\n+     bundle_version: 1.2.3\\n+     stage: prod\\n</code></pre>\\n<h2>Build metadata</h2>\\n<p>The plugin tags every uploaded file with <code>build.name</code>, <code>build.number</code>, <code>build.url</code> and <code>vcs.revision</code>, and uses the same build to fill a release bundle. The values come from the pipeline environment unless you set them explicitly:</p>\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Setting</th>\\n<th>Woodpecker</th>\\n<th>Drone</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody><tr>\\n<td><code>build_name</code></td>\\n<td><code>CI_REPO</code></td>\\n<td><code>DRONE_REPO</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>build_number</code></td>\\n<td><code>CI_PIPELINE_NUMBER</code></td>\\n<td><code>DRONE_BUILD_NUMBER</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>build_url</code></td>\\n<td><code>CI_PIPELINE_URL</code></td>\\n<td><code>DRONE_BUILD_LINK</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>vcs_revision</code></td>\\n<td><code>CI_COMMIT_SHA</code></td>\\n<td><code>DRONE_COMMIT_SHA</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>bundle_name</code></td>\\n<td><code>CI_REPO_NAME</code></td>\\n<td><code>DRONE_REPO_NAME</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><code>bundle_version</code></td>\\n<td><code>CI_COMMIT_TAG</code></td>\\n<td><code>DRONE_TAG</code></td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table>\\n<h2>Parameter Reference</h2>\\n<p>server\\n: OpenArtifact server URL, for example <code>https://artifacts.example.com</code></p>\\n<p>token\\n: API token with write access to the repository. Always pass it with <code>from_secret</code>; the plugin hands it to <code>oa</code> through the environment and never prints it</p>\\n<p>action\\n: <code>upload</code> (default), <code>bundle</code>, <code>promote</code> or <code>upload+promote</code>. <code>upload</code> uploads <code>files</code>. <code>bundle</code> creates the bundle <code>bundle_name</code>/<code>bundle_version</code>, adds the artifacts of this build (and <code>bundle_paths</code>) and seals it. <code>promote</code> promotes an existing sealed bundle to <code>stage</code>. <code>upload+promote</code> runs upload, bundle and promote in order and stops at the first failure</p>\\n<p>repo\\n: target repository. Uploads work on path based repositories (raw, maven, ivy, sbt, deb, rpm); for other formats use the native client</p>\\n<p>files\\n: list of files or glob patterns to upload, relative to the workspace</p>\\n<p>target_path\\n: path prefix inside the repository</p>\\n<p>flat\\n: upload files without their local directories</p>\\n<p>properties\\n: map of extra artifact properties, for example <code>team: core</code></p>\\n<p>build_name\\n: build name property, defaults to the repository full name</p>\\n<p>build_number\\n: build number property, defaults to the pipeline number</p>\\n<p>build_url\\n: build URL property, defaults to the pipeline URL</p>\\n<p>vcs_revision\\n: commit SHA property, defaults to the pipeline commit</p>\\n<p>bundle_name\\n: release bundle name, defaults to the repository name</p>\\n<p>bundle_version\\n: release bundle version, defaults to the tag of a tag pipeline</p>\\n<p>bundle_description\\n: release bundle description</p>\\n<p>bundle_pipeline\\n: name of the promotion pipeline the bundle follows. Promotion needs a pipeline that defines <code>stage</code> (and, unless the stage fixes a repository, <code>target_repo</code>)</p>\\n<p>bundle_paths\\n: additional paths inside <code>repo</code> to add to the bundle</p>\\n<p>gpg_key\\n: GPG key id used to seal the bundle</p>\\n<p>stage\\n: promotion stage, required for <code>promote</code> and <code>upload+promote</code></p>\\n<p>target_repo\\n: repository the promoted items are copied into</p>\\n<p>notes\\n: promotion notes</p>\\n<p>result_file\\n: write a JSON result (success, uploaded files, bundle state, per step output) to this path. It is also written when the step fails</p>\\n<p>oa_path\\n: path of the <code>oa</code> binary, default <code>oa</code> (the image ships a verified release of it)</p>\\n<h2>Result</h2>\\n<p>The step log lists every uploaded file with size and checksum, the bundle state and the promotion. The exit code is non-zero if any <code>oa</code> call fails or if the installed <code>oa</code> is older than 0.10.0.</p>\\n","tags":["publish","artifacts","release"],"author":"openartifact","containerImage":"ghcr.io/openartifact/drone-openartifact","containerImageUrl":"https://github.com/openartifact/drone-openartifact/pkgs/container/drone-openartifact","verified":false,"iconDataUrl":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,"}')}}]);